# Build context for images built from the repo root. Only apps/web/Dockerfile.runtime does that (docker-compose.prod.yml
# web service); every other image has its own context (apps/api, apps/source-sim, apps/web) and its own .dockerignore.
# Allow-list: everything is out except the web app's sources and the demo it extracts its stylesheet and photos from.
*
!apps/web
!fixtures/demo

# inside the allowed folders: secrets, dependencies, build output, generated files (the build regenerates them), tests
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/node_modules
apps/web/dist
apps/web/src/styles/legacy.gen.css
apps/web/public/assets/products
apps/web/*.tsbuildinfo
apps/web/coverage
apps/web/e2e
apps/web/playwright-report
apps/web/test-results
apps/web/**/*.test.ts
apps/web/**/*.test.tsx
apps/web/.dockerignore
apps/web/Dockerfile*
